642dd436-ab8f-49d5-9640-8a2f2ee0fdd8","position":{"commit_sha":"db2f2f0083657d212f15837781ded61075f3efb2","position":"1787027131357088001-642dd436-ab8f-49d5-9640-8a2f2ee0fdd8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"53ccd5cfb813b8433cda45927126b75ab2b367411626c5f05eaa631d7083a847","event_uuid":"3c032539-3560-43c3-9dae-3508f2cb83c7","position":{"commit_sha":"319a8a899ae76128a79374bf3069d452cb2c487e","position":"1787027230899582001-3c032539-3560-43c3-9dae-3508f2cb83c7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation evidence (2026-08-17): installed the lock-compatible optional dependency `jira==3.10.5` into this dedicated worktree venv and inspected the runtime API without reading credentials or contacting Jira. `inspect.signature(jira.JIRA.__init__)` exposes top-level `max_retries: int = 3`. Source assigns `self._session.max_retries = max_retries`. A no-network construction probe using `JIRA(server=\"https://jira.invalid\", token_auth=\"probe\", get_server_info=False, max_retries=0)` produced `_session.max_retries == 0`. This confirms the dedicated executor-client mechanism and shows that the existing transport comment about `verify` belonging in the options dict does not apply to `max_retries`. The remediated plan review then certified PASS at origin/main SHA 5b5008bbfbec04cd8c0c9ad2d4b2860ed7d8f652.","timestamp":1787027230899582001}],"created_at":1787022532234587001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"456581fc-1006-4f33-9e62-abec02381228","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e042-4780-6c63-4b09"},{"link_uuid":"30f1e3b2-d609-446f-ab33-7beb0aa15733","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6"}],"description":"## Context / Outcome\nCurrent Jira writes can cross generic dispatch retry, Cloud ACLI/REST retry, or Jira DC SDK/wrapper retry. A timeout can multiply writes or leave acceptance ambiguous. Prove one provider-neutral logical-operation budget by setting an exact summary through Cloud and DC. Jira has no Rebar idempotency key, so recovery observes desired state before replay. S1 establishes ADR 0100; S3 owns production cutover and terminal-outcome consumption; S5 finalizes the ADR after all operation families migrate.\n\n## Approach\n1. Define an operation/outcome contract: stable logical id, desired postcondition, invocation/request counts, disposition, failure scope, replay safety, provider delay, `retry_not_before`, and bounded redacted diagnostics.\n2. One physical invocation is one executor call to a write or observation; raw requests are counted separately. Allow at most three invocations and 15 seconds cumulative sleep. Use `2**(attempt+1) + U[0,1)`: [2s,3s), then [4s,5s). Provider `Retry-After`, parsed by `_errors.parse_retry_after`, is a lower bound.\n3. Add a constructor-injected internal route selector at dispatch. It defaults to legacy in S1; tests explicitly select the executor. It is not config or an environment variable. Only exact `{\"summary\"}` is eligible; mixed fields remain one legacy call. No dual-send. S3 owns venue-gated validation and default-on cutover.\n4. Cloud makes one ACLI process per write and preserves existing POSIX/non-POSIX cleanup. Decode sanitized exit/stdout/stderr; unknown shapes fail loud. Recovery uses primary-store `get_issue_by_rest`, never ACLI JQL. Add a per-call policy to `acli_rest._rest_urlopen_with_retry`; summary recovery alone selects one attempt/no sleep. All existing callers retain three attempts with 2s/5s waits.\n5. Build a dedicated DC executor client with `jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0)` plus a session guard. The legacy client keeps current SDK retry. Selected pre-read/write/read-back calls use `_with_connection_retry` under a per-call one-attempt/no-sleep policy; legacy callers keep current behavior.\n6. A DC summary-write invocation is GET -> PUT -> GET, with no hidden repeats. Failure ends that invocation. Successful read-back is authoritative. After ambiguous PUT, a separate GET observation consumes the next invocation.\n7. Desired summary observed after timeout means recovered success. Conclusive old state may replay within the remaining budget. Failed, rate-limited, or inconclusive observation returns non-replaying `commit_unknown`. An authoritative delay that cannot fit returns `retry_not_before` without sleeping. Auth, TLS, permission, invalid request, and permanent failures do not retry; eligible network, 429, and retryable 5xx failures use the shared schedule.\n8. Preserve the `update_one` / `apply_handlers.handle_update` boundary while S1 is test-only. `dispatch_one` maps success/recovered success to the legacy result and fills `_fields_synced` only after conclusive success; `_comment_errors` and `_subop` keep their shapes. `commit_unknown`/`retry_not_before` map to a tagged internal result. `handle_update` records a bounded per-mutation error/disposition, leaves `_fields_synced` empty, advances no baseline or set-field provenance, persists no deferral in S1, and lets the batch continue. S3 maps terminal dispositions to pass/fuse control and durable deferral, then retires the bridge.\n9. Emit one bounded redacted completion log for terminal/exhausted outcomes and cleanup failure.\n10. ADR 0100 records the retry owner, Jira idempotency limit, observe-before-replay, budget, lifecycle owners, rollback, and deltas from ADR 0084/0087 and desired-state ADRs 0004/0026/0029. The 15-second cumulative limit supersedes ADR 0084 only on selected routes.\n\n## Scope\n- Core: `operation_outcome.py`, `retry_budget.py`, `dispatch_one.py`, `dispatch_apply_phases.py`, `apply_handlers.py`.\n- Cloud: `acli.py`, `acli_subprocess.py`, `acli_rest.py`, backend; preserve unrelated REST retry defaults.\n- DC: `transport.py`, `retry.py`, `_issues.py`, backend; dedicated executor client and per-call policy preserve legacy defaults.\n- ADR 0100; budget/outcome, handler, historical ACLI, cleanup, and DC request tests.\n\n## Testing\nFake-clock/stateful tests cover schedules, deadlines, request order, ambiguity, recovery, 429/503, malformed delay, auth/TLS/permanent errors, and no real sleep. Poison tests reject generic retry, inner Cloud/DC retry, SDK retry, or extra ACLI processes; neighbor tests preserve unselected behavior. Handler tests prevent false success/baseline/provenance. Sanitized historical triples pin decoding; real process tests pin cleanup; output tests pin redaction and size. All required tests are local and credential-free. S3 owns venue-gated cutover evidence; S5 owns final live confirmation.\n\n## Compatibility / Rollback\nProduction stays on legacy in S1 through the internal selector. Rollback selects legacy before a call; no new config, env surface, or dual-send exists. S3 changes the default only after validation. Selected-route deltas are the three-invocation/15-second budget, long-delay deferral, fail-loud unknown ACLI shapes, and non-replaying inconclusive recovery. Other callers retain current retry behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cloud and DC summary routes produce one provider-neutral outcome schema; tests assert every field.\n- [ ] Repeated invocations preserve one logical id.\n- [ ] No selected operation exceeds three invocations or 15 seconds cumulative sleep.\n- [ ] Each selected DC write invocation is exactly GET/PUT/GET with no hidden repeats.\n- [ ] Cloud recovery performs one primary-store REST request with no sleep; neighbor tests preserve existing REST retry.\n- [ ] Executor-selected exact `{\"summary\"}` bypasses generic `_call_with_retry`.\n- [ ] The constructor selector defaults to legacy, adds no config/env key, and tests explicitly enable it.\n- [ ] Mixed fields stay one unsplit legacy call.\n- [ ] Confirmed outcomes preserve legacy result, `_fields_synced`, `_comment_errors`, and `_subop` shapes.\n- [ ] Terminal outcomes record bounded per-mutation errors with no baseline/provenance advance or S1 deferral.\n- [ ] ADR and contract name S3 as sole cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and bridge-retirement owner.\n- [ ] The dedicated DC executor client uses guarded `max_retries=0`; legacy SDK retry is unchanged.\n- [ ] Selected DC wrapper calls are one-attempt/no-sleep; legacy wrapper behavior is unchanged.\n- [ ] Fallback sleeps remain [2s,3s), then [4s,5s).\n- [ ] Over-budget provider delay returns `retry_not_before` without sleep.\n- [ ] Permanent failures use one invocation; eligible transient failures use the schedule.\n- [ ] Satisfied observation returns recovered success without another write.\n- [ ] Conclusive old state permits only remaining-budget replay.\n- [ ] Failed/inconclusive observation returns non-replaying `commit_unknown`.\n- [ ] ACLI cleanup passes for POSIX groups and non-POSIX children.\n- [ ] Historical ACLI triples decode deterministically; unknown triples do not retry.\n- [ ] Completion logs are bounded, redacted, and expose terminal/exhausted outcomes.\n- [ ] ADR 0100 records contract, ownership, compatibility deltas, rollback, and prior art; index checks pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/operation_outcome.py","reason":"Provider-neutral logical-operation outcomes and terminal dispositions."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/retry_budget.py","reason":"Single three-invocation and fifteen-second sleep budget."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"Legacy-default selector, selected summary route, and compatibility result mapping."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"Bypass and poison-test the legacy generic retry wrapper."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Consume terminal result tags without false baseline or provenance advance."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"Expose the selected Cloud summary operation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"One-process invocation, decoding, timeout, and cleanup."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_rest.py","reason":"Per-call single-attempt recovery observation while preserving other retry defaults."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","reason":"Expose the typed Cloud operation to core coordination."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","reason":"Build a dedicated no-SDK-retry executor client without changing legacy construction."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py","reason":"Per-call one-attempt executor policy while preserving legacy wrapper defaults."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","reason":"Execute the selected DC summary postcondition once per invocation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"Expose the typed DC operation to core coordination."},{"path":"docs/adr/0100-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Establish coordination, retry, ambiguity, lifecycle ownership, and rollback."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py","reason":"Fake-clock budget, route, classification, ambiguity, and wire-count tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py","reason":"Regression tests for result compatibility and no false baseline or provenance advance."},{"path":"tests/fixtures/reconciler/rp03_acli_outcomes.json","reason":"Sanitized historical ACLI exit/stdout/stderr evidence."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py","reason":"Preserve timeout termination and process-group reaping."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_auth_failure.py","reason":"Reuse captured real unauthorized output in the outcome corpus."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_dc_transport_heldout.py","reason":"Prove dedicated max_retries=0 construction and legacy-policy preservation."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","4217-d1d6-370b-4e98"],["relates_to","6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6"],["relates_to","e042-4780-6c63-4b09"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"4217-d1d6-370b-4e98","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp03","reconciler","jira","retry","tdd"],"ticket_id":"f5ac-6373-5e33-4374","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-03 S1 — Execute one Jira postcondition through a single retry budget","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_retry.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC11","dd_text":"Typed route, internal selector, result compatibility, attempt accounting, Cloud observation, and terminal lifecycle ownership"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_auth_failure.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py -k \"log or acli or reap or cleanup\"","dd_id":"AC20-AC22","dd_text":"Cross-platform ACLI cleanup, historical decoding, and bounded redacted operation logs"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_dc_transport_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_rate_limit_retry_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py -k \"dc or cloud_observation or legacy_retry\"","dd_id":"AC4-AC5,AC12-AC19","dd_text":"DC request shape, per-call retry policies, preserved legacy defaults, provider classification, and ambiguous recovery"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC23","dd_text":"ADR numbering and documentation index"}]},"source_event_uuids":["882691a5-e3fa-490e-817b-fe26abe41c47","e4b2983b-8f0a-4365-bd13-675dd9f3fddb","4c25b1bc-3251-412a-a288-112de0b3b2a5","127f84f8-9d2f-4838-b2eb-a85d3a178937","b9fc38a0-c549-4be0-baba-cd05f1df0267","96303163-f277-4ad0-8582-eeb8f6c024d4","194790a2-f612-46a8-8c8a-27dbeef7bbf9","9e7ccb57-5362-4a64-bfb8-b7b7c761b343","43200afb-f723-4898-a8ef-75fc5977190d","9548c94f-6646-4a16-bf69-621a1065c797","3b6038bf-e430-4e78-8b39-382a0684f517","43b8942a-adb4-4ac8-8988-862842353ba6","3c86ff2e-b1ca-463b-8b7b-9cb62f6c49a5","01fd755d-17c1-4c60-8d61-f2958692a81b","0d22ae13-5981-4134-87b3-1eda5442c648","eb059fbb-03a3-4234-b830-7f4d7b7966ee","642dd436-ab8f-49d5-9640-8a2f2ee0fdd8","3c032539-3560-43c3-9dae-3508f2cb83c7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787029935944440001,"uuid":"55991ba3-3f87-4015-a48c-cdae70da0ffb"}